🚀 The feature, motivation and pitch
When I tried to call torch.linalg.eigvals with another acceleration device, I found that an error was reported. After preliminary location, it is found that when complex_out is used to construct a complex number, some input tensors are on the device and some are on the CPU.
if (values.is_complex()) {
      values = at::complex_out(values, real_values, imag_values); //values is on the device,but real_values and imag_values are on the CPU
} else {
      TORCH_CHECK(false, "torch.linalg.eig: imaginary part of eigenvalues is non-zero, can't safely cast eigenvalues to non-complex dtype.")
 }

Finally, I found the root cause,pytorch\aten\src\ATen\native\BatchLinearAlgebra.cpp:
  // because MAGMA's GEEV takes CPU inputs and returns CPU outputs
  // 'values' tensor that is on GPU device can't be used directly
  values_tmp_needed |= values.is_cuda(); //Look, it only checks if the acceleration device is cuda.
  ...
  if (values_tmp_needed) { 
    Tensor values_tmp = at::empty({0}, options.dtype(values_type));
    std::tie(values_tmp, std::ignore) = linalg_eig_out_info(input, values_tmp, vectors, infos, /*compute_eigenvectors=*/false);
    at::native::resize_output(values, values_tmp.sizes());
    values.copy_(values_tmp);
  } else { // use 'values' storage directly
    std::tie(values, std::ignore) = linalg_eig_out_info(input, values, vectors, infos, /*compute_eigenvectors=*/false);
  }

In linalg_eig_out, temporary variables are set when the device is determined to be a CUDA device, and temporary variables on the CPU are used as input. However, when other acceleration devices are used, the corresponding judgment is not performed. The input is still the tensor on the device.  I would appreciate it if the community would consider compatibility with other devices in response to this issue!
Alternatives
Maybe you can determine whether values and vectors are on the CPU. If values and vectors are not on the CPU, set temporary variables on the CPU as subsequent input.
Additional context
No response
